- op: discuss  # fbd7
  at: '2026-06-25T17:53:48Z'  # fbd7
  by: agent  # fbd7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fbd7
  clock: 11  # fbd7
  nonce: fbd7  # fbd7
  message: "Implemented in commit 0a3fbb77cf (origin/dev) per the 2026-06-25 human ruling. File-locality split out of call_construct into a new registered edge.meta key call_locality (axis_meta_keys.py, AXIS_EDGE_META, ADR-0024). bash.py + objc.py now write meta={'call_locality':'cross_file'} on cross-file calls and no longer write call_construct there (it only ever held the locality misuse — no construct value lost). Sparse per convention: cross_file stamped on boundary-crossing calls; absent = same-file. Behavioral evidence — production-path tests: test_bash.py::test_extracts_cross_file_call_edges and test_objc.py::test_extracts_cross_file_call_edges now assert the cross-file edge carries meta['call_locality']=='cross_file' AND 'call_construct' not in meta. 100% coverage; full affected suite 10831 passed."  # fbd7
